    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "1be09b7327f53c41ec1ddeb0df08bf5ff3380cc4e86591a88f95806430da11fa",
      "text": "After leaving Cancún, your first stop is Tulum. This port was an important Maya trading centre. It stands on a cliff above the Caribbean Sea, and goods were distributed from here to the interior of the Yucatán Peninsula.\n\nThe archaeological site is fairly small, but its setting makes Tulum particularly memorable. You'll see the defensive wall, temples, surviving murals and reliefs.\n\nNext, travel to Bacalar Lagoon, part of a natural system of lagoons and rivers where the water changes colour from silvery turquoise to violet.\n\nFrom Bacalar, continue to Xpujil, a Maya archaeological site in the state of Campeche. The earliest settlements here date to around 400 BCE. Xpujil flourished between 500 and 750 CE, and the city declined around 1100.\n\nSpend the night at a 4-star hotel near the ruins.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-mw9gatwi",
        "model": "ChatGPT Codex"
      }
    },
